    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d750">

                <pb facs="0835" n="723" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg723"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 24172/6.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Ambassador Wilson.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-06-01"><hi rendition="#italic">June 1,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Informs him that the California authorities find it impossible to convict Leodoro
                    Garcia, who is now in jail under provisional detention at Jalostotitlan,
                    Jalisco, under name of Eledoro Garcia, of murder. Says that a new warrant of
                    arrest has been issued for <pb facs="0836" n="724" xml:id="pg724"/> Leodoro
                    Garcia for crime of assault with intent to commit murder committed in
                    California, April 25, 1909, upon person of Louis Manzo. Directs him immediately
                    to request provisional arrest and detention on this charge.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
